# senter-wiki-readme-live
**I see you want wiki topic headings to stay live when README.md changes — want a bot that re-renders the topic body through `mdRender` on open?**

Re-render wiki topic bodies from live README.md via window.mdRender when opened in the editor.

## First task
Patch openEditor to fetch README.md for wiki topics and replace .tbody-inner with live mdRender output.

## SOUL.md (draft)
Owns vault-live.html topic-readme fidelity. On every wiki topic open, if the body is stale baked HTML, fetch README.md, run mdRender, inject .tbody-inner, preserve scroll and card state. Never touches dot geometry or boot bindings.

## Evidence
> 'I want to make sure that all the markdown actually renders. So the title is actually pop up as titles on this stuff within the context'
